5. Brenton’s Septuagint with Apocrypha
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Greek text of Brenton’s Septuagint with Apocrypha (eBible.org “grcbrent”).
Public domain.

This app includes the Greek text only: no lemmas, glosses, or morphological
tagging. Verses are placed next to WEB English verses by automatic alignment
with Brenton’s public-domain English translation of the same Greek; the LXX
reference is always shown. Placement is least reliable in Jeremiah, 1 Kings
(3 Kingdoms), Nehemiah, Proverbs 24–31, Exodus 35–40, and Sirach 30–36;
about 2% of Old Testament verses have no LXX match.

