11. Studies and texts not included
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Guided Studies in this app present a named author’s position in original
lesson notes written for Hive Scribe. They do not reproduce copyrighted
book text. The first bundled study, “The Oneness of God,” follows the
chapter titles and order of David K. Bernard, The Oneness of God (Word
Aflame Press, 1983). Lesson summaries, reflection questions, and verse
notes are original to this app. Scripture is cited from the World English
Bible (public domain).

Hebrew and Aramaic fragments that exist but are not packaged here are
not invented: Sirach is known in Hebrew for about two-thirds of the book
(Cairo Geniza, Masada, and related finds); Tobit is attested in Aramaic
and Hebrew fragments from Qumran; a Greek fragment of the Letter of
Jeremiah (Baruch 6) is known as 7Q2. This app uses the Brenton Septuagint
(and the Vulgate where aligned) for those books, not those fragments.

