14. King James Version (1769) with the Apocrypha (default English text)
     Public domain (outside the United Kingdom)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Source: eBible.org "eng-kjv" (King James Version + Apocrypha),
https://ebible.org/Scriptures/eng-kjv_vpl.zip, "The King James Version or
Authorized Version of the Holy Bible, using the standardized text of 1769,
with Apocrypha/Deuterocanon", brought "courtesy of the Crosswire Bible
Society and eBible.org". eBible.org marks it "Public Domain" and states:
"Letters patent issued by King James with no expiration date means that to
print this translation in the United Kingdom or import printed copies into
the UK, you need permission. Currently, the Cambridge University Press, the
Oxford University Press, and Collins have the exclusive right to print this
Bible translation in the UK. This royal decree has no effect outside of the
UK, where this work is firmly in the Public Domain."

The wording is unaltered. Words the translators supplied (bracketed in the
source) are shown in italics. The KJV is placed on the app's verse labels
(WEB numbering) so the original-language layers stay aligned; where the KJV
numbers differently its own reference is shown (Romans 16:25-27 at
14:24-26; the Rest of Esther in Greek Esther; the Song of the Three
Children, Susanna and Bel in Daniel 3, 13 and 14; a few Sirach verses;
2 Esdras 7). Placement in those books was done automatically by comparing
the KJV with the WEB. 3 and 4 Maccabees and Psalm 151 are not in the KJV
and are shown in the WEB. The WEB remains selectable in Settings and the
reading bar.

